{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1184405-which-story-tier-do-you-play-the-most","id":1184405,"title":"Which story tier do you play the most?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-10T08:23:29-08:00","id":1184405,"title":"Which story tier do you play the most?","content":"In CoD (and back in nWoD), there is the concept of tiers of play, differentiating between how intimate or how epic your stories can be. Here tier 1 is entirely personal or street level, whereas tier 4 encompasses epic stories, where the shape of the universe is at stake.<br /> <br /> Which tier are typically your games (an for which splats?) Are there some tier/splat combinations which you have tried and didn't really work out (or worked out surprisingly well)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-10-2018, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T11:36:52-08:00","id":1184458,"title":"","content":"I've played or run Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Changeling and Hunter.<br /> <br /> For the most part, we do first or second tier, which is Local, and Regional, going by Chronicles of Darkness' descriptions. Previous books I think have described them differently. Anyways it's either dealing with intensely personal stuff, or stuff that affects the city they're in. Recently, with Mage, I made my last game Global with some Cosmic implications, and I believe the other STs in our group are interested in playing around with different tiers.<br /> <br /> I think a lot is going to depend on what you want to play. Cosmic stuff can lose a lot of the personal, so you're not playing a traditional character who perhaps is trying to balance their supernatural life with their romantic relationship. Some games handle that better. In all cases they're pretty different, once you move up two or three spaces on the tiers, with vampires going from worrying about perhaps someone saw them drinking that waitress, to having loyal servants ensuring they're fed each day while they manipulate the world.<br /> <br /> This shouldn't be a surprise but so far the only games that are really easy to do high-tier stuff are the ones that have supplements for high-tier stuff. Mage, Vampire, maybe Demon. Werewolf has always alluded to a lot of global events but it hasn't really had the support for that kind of stuff, with how to deal with Rank 6+ entities or how annihilating one of said beings would impact the world..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T12:23:34-08:00","id":1184481,"title":"","content":"I always strive to do tier-1, street level, the characters are small fish in a big pond kind of deal. <br /> ...<br /> And i always fail spectacularly and default back to ''the fate of the city hang in the balance and only the PC can do something about it...'' sigh<br /> One day i'll succeed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T14:22:17-08:00","id":1184514,"title":"","content":"Run or play?<br /> <br /> I tend to run Tier 1, but I always manage end up in Tier 3 games when I play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T15:22:43-08:00","id":1184910,"title":"","content":"Almost exclusively Tier 1 games, although they tend to escalate to Tier 2 naturally if they go on a long time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T16:17:15-08:00","id":1186863,"title":"","content":"I'm a little bit split in my games. The thing that really draws me to CoD is the way it emphasizes local stories that are personal to the characters. I really don't care for &quot;saving the world&quot; style plot lines. On the other hand, I really love lore and world building, so the ideas I like to play around with tend to be cosmic - exploring the realms invisible, interacting with gods, and finding the weird, crazy ideas deep in a game line or in the spaces between them. <br /> <br /> So my games tend to be tier 1, but often touch on tier 4, and I frequently try to bridge those scales - either by making a deeply personal quest take place in a cosmic arena, or by re-contextualizing a cosmic problem with its impact on the PCs personal lives.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here's a breakdown of the games I've been in, for those who are interested:<br /> <br /> I've run a two year werewolf game that I think stayed tier 1 the whole time. We started with the &quot;Manitou Springs&quot; SAS and just kept going. It touched on other packs and had a road-trip quest or two, but never really hit regional problems. But I did have a player trying to make peace with the Pure, and introduced some weird creatures to play with / introduce lore - such as [my homebrew of] other changing breeds and their mythologies, a Claimed pretending to be a shifter, a Weird Thing trying to fabricate human spirits, mages, GM infrastructure, idigam, spirit-slaving sorcerers, and Purified.<br /> <br /> I ran a long term Dresden files game that focused on tier 1 stories, but with tier 3 &amp; 4 implications: the PCs, apprentice mages at the first attempt at a magic boarding school, were being groomed into being necromancers so that they could summon an abyssal realm... so that really shook up politics and threatened the world, but it was done through the very personal ways they were being manipulated. <br /> <br /> I ran a short, focused, really fun CtL game that was inspired by CtD. It was a tier 4 story and problem, but played out in a tier 1 way - how a cosmic problem affect the PCs and loved ones. It started with the conceit that Arcadia was structured and coherent - the place we're living stories exist - and all that was falling apart as stories consumed each other and hybridized. But all the threats came through personal relationships: your gf is a fetch, your former keeper just got exiled, your mentor got recaptured, your enemy is asking for asylum.<br /> <br /> A while ago I played in a few cWoD games... those are hard to judge, because an Apocalypse always seems to creep in. The werewolf games were tier 2, until the finale; then there was a crossover game that was, I think, entirely tier 1 - the &quot;apocalypse&quot; in that was the city slowly sinking into the underworld.<br /> <br /> I've also been a player in a long running tier 1 CtL game. In my experience, that one is pretty easy to keep tier 1, as even trips into Arcadia and otherworldly incursions tend to be very personal to the PCs.<br /> <br /> I'm currently running a tier 1 and 4 crossover game. The PCs are, in part, focused on taking over supernatural crime in their city, but also have cosmic goals of rescuing a soul from the afterlife and destroying an Exarch and his cult. So our stories either swing between the tiers or try to bridge them.<br /> <br /> I'm also running a Dresden Files game right now which is focusing on tier 1 stories, but with tier 3 implications - the chronicle's major threat is the existence of magic being revealed to mortals, and it's taking place in London, where we can see both the plays of global powers and the impact on everyday people and minor talents.<br /> <br /> I am preparing for a future mummy game that will be a tier 2 game: trying to shape an entire country across 3000 years to align with Irem's model.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I guess that's a lot of examples, but tl:dr, I personally love to explore weird parts of the lore and get deep into cosmic concepts and exploring the realms invisible. But I, and my players, love the way CoD emphasizes personal stories and motivations, keeping it close to the PCs. So even when I use cosmic stuff, I try to give it a personal context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}